  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Rotate In\n\nText swings into place: spinning in plane (z) or hinged in depth on the x or y axis, with a small scale-up and a fade that leads the move.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 3 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A headline, badge or title card should arrive with a rotation: a spin for marks, a hinge for panels.\n- One short phrase needs an entrance with more character than a fade.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You want per-letter motion: use split-text-chars or per-character-rise.\n- Several lines should reveal one after another: use mask-reveal-up.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"Swing into place.\"\n- font_size (number, 24-260): Font size, default 84\n- color (color): Color, default \"#f4f4f5\"\n- font_weight (number, 100-900): Font weight, default 700\n- font (enum): Font, default \"geist\"\n- degrees (number, -180-180): Angle, default -12\n- axis (enum): Axis, default \"z\"\n- perspective (number, 200-4000): Perspective, default 1200\n- scale_from (number, 0.2-1.5): Scale from, default 0.96\n- origin (enum): Pivot, default \"center\"\n- duration_frames (number, 4-120): Duration, default 30\n- delay_frames (number, 0-120): Delay, default 6\n- exit (boolean): Exit, default true\n\nSource: https://github.com/riaz37/remotion-ui. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Rotate In\n\n  Swings into place in plane, or hinged in depth on the x or y axis.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/riaz37/remotion-ui/blob/0aecaca2b61a167992e1205d10e4da16d8a71331/apps/web/registry/bases/default/primitives/rotate-in.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 RemotionUI\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"rotate-in\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"3\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"text\",\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"role\": \"content\",\n        \"label\": \"Text\",\n        \"description\": \"The text. A line break starts a new line.\",\n        \"default\": \"Swing into place.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"font_size\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Font size\",\n        \"description\": \"Text size in pixels.\",\n        \"default\": 84,\n        \"min\": 24,\n        \"max\": 260,\n        \"step\": 1,\n        \"unit\": \"px\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"color\",\n        \"type\": \"color\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Color\",\n        \"description\": \"Text color.\",\n        \"default\": \"#f4f4f5\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"font_weight\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Font weight\",\n        \"description\": \"Weight of the text.\",\n        \"default\": 700,\n        \"min\": 100,\n        \"max\": 900,\n        \"step\": 100\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"font\",\n        \"type\": \"enum\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Font\",\n        \"description\": \"Typeface.\",\n        \"default\": \"geist\",\n        \"options\": [\n          {\n            \"value\": \"geist\",\n            \"label\": \"Geist\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"poppins\",\n            \"label\": \"Poppins\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"playfair\",\n            \"label\": \"Playfair Display\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"grotesk\",\n            \"label\": \"Space Grotesk\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"degrees\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Angle\",\n        \"description\": \"Angle the text starts at, in degrees. Negative tilts anticlockwise.\",\n        \"default\": -12,\n        \"min\": -180,\n        \"max\": 180,\n        \"step\": 1,\n        \"unit\": \"deg\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"axis\",\n        \"type\": \"enum\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Axis\",\n        \"description\": \"z spins in plane; x and y hinge in depth.\",\n        \"default\": \"z\",\n        \"options\": [\n          {\n            \"value\": \"z\",\n            \"label\": \"In plane (z)\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"x\",\n            \"label\": \"Hinge on x\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"y\",\n            \"label\": \"Hinge on y\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"perspective\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Perspective\",\n        \"description\": \"Depth of the 3D projection for the x and y axes, in pixels.\",\n        \"default\": 1200,\n        \"min\": 200,\n        \"max\": 4000,\n        \"step\": 50,\n        \"unit\": \"px\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"scale_from\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Scale from\",\n        \"description\": \"Scale at the start; a rotation that also grows reads as one gesture.\",\n        \"default\": 0.96,\n        \"min\": 0.2,\n        \"max\": 1.5,\n        \"step\": 0.01\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"origin\",\n        \"type\": \"enum\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Pivot\",\n        \"description\": \"Point the rotation pivots around.\",\n        \"default\": \"center\",\n        \"options\": [\n          {\n            \"value\": \"center\",\n            \"label\": \"Center\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"top\",\n            \"label\": \"Top\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"bottom\",\n            \"label\": \"Bottom\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"left\",\n            \"label\": \"Left\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"right\",\n            \"label\": \"Right\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"top left\",\n            \"label\": \"Top left\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"top right\",\n            \"label\": \"Top right\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"bottom left\",\n            \"label\": \"Bottom left\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"bottom right\",\n            \"label\": \"Bottom right\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"duration_frames\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Duration\",\n        \"description\": \"Frames (30 per second) the entrance takes.\",\n        \"default\": 30,\n        \"min\": 4,\n        \"max\": 120,\n        \"step\": 1,\n        \"unit\": \"frames\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"delay_frames\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Delay\",\n        \"description\": \"Frames before the entrance starts.\",\n        \"default\": 6,\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 120,\n        \"step\": 1,\n        \"unit\": \"frames\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"exit\",\n        \"type\": \"boolean\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Exit\",\n        \"description\": \"Play an exit at the end of the clip.\",\n        \"default\": true\n      }\n    ]\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Rotate In</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@100..900&amp;family=Poppins:wght@400;600;800&amp;family=Playfair+Display:wght@400..900&amp;family=Space+Grotesk:wght@300..700&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        #root { color: #f4f4f5; }\n        .rti-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n        .rti-text { max-width: 88%; text-align: center; line-height: 1.15; white-space: pre-wrap; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"rotate-in\" data-duration=\"3\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"rti-clip\" class=\"rti-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"3\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div id=\"rti-text\" class=\"rti-text\" role=\"img\"></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars = window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables() : {};\n            function num(v, f, min, max) { var n = Number(v); return Number.isFinite(n) && v !== \"\" && v !== null ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : f; }\n            function str(v, f) { return typeof v === \"string\" && v.trim() ? v : f; }\n            function bool(v, f) { if (v === undefined || v === null || v === \"\") return f; return !(v === false || v === \"false\" || v === 0 || v === \"0\"); }\n            function pick(v, list, f) { v = String(v); return list.indexOf(v) >= 0 ? v : f; }\n            function clamp01(v) { return v < 0 ? 0 : v > 1 ? 1 : v; }\n            function lerp(a, b, t) { return a + (b - a) * t; }\n            function ramp(v, a, b, from, to, ease) { var p = b === a ? 1 : clamp01((v - a) / (b - a)); if (ease) p = ease(p); return from + (to - from) * p; }\n            function bez(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n              return function (x) {\n                if (x <= 0) return 0;\n                if (x >= 1) return 1;\n                var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n                for (var i = 0; i < 30; i++) {\n                  var cx = 3 * (1 - t) * (1 - t) * t * x1 + 3 * (1 - t) * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n                  if (cx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n                  t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                }\n                return 3 * (1 - t) * (1 - t) * t * y1 + 3 * (1 - t) * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n              };\n            }\n            function mulberry32(a) { return function () { a |= 0; a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0; var t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a); t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t; return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; }; }\n            function mk(tag, parent, cls, text) { var e = document.createElement(tag); if (cls) e.className = cls; if (text !== undefined) e.textContent = text; if (parent) parent.appendChild(e); return e; }\n            var TOTAL = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"3\");\n            // Every frame is drawn from the frame number alone, so seeking anywhere draws the same frame.\n            function drive(name, frameFn) {\n              var clock = { f: 0 };\n              var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n              tl.to(clock, { f: TOTAL * 30, duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { frameFn(clock.f); } }, 0);\n              frameFn(0);\n              tl.seek(0);\n              window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n              window.__timelines[name] = tl;\n            }\n\n            var FONTS = { geist: \"Geist, system-ui, sans-serif\", poppins: \"Poppins, system-ui, sans-serif\", playfair: '\"Playfair Display\", Georgia, serif', grotesk: '\"Space Grotesk\", system-ui, sans-serif' };\n            var fontKey = pick(vars.font, [\"geist\", \"poppins\", \"playfair\", \"grotesk\"], \"geist\");\n            root.style.fontFamily = FONTS[fontKey];\n            var ARRIVE = bez(0.33, 1, 0.68, 1), ENTER = bez(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);\n            function EXIT(t) { return t * t * t; }\n            // Enter/exit contract of the source library's motion primitives: light leads the move (opacity done 55 % in), an exit is shorter and accelerates away.\n            function enterExit(frame, o) {\n              var et = clamp01((frame - o.delay) / o.duration);\n              var motion = ARRIVE(et), opacity = ENTER(clamp01(et / 0.55));\n              if (!o.exit) return { motion: motion, opacity: opacity, exiting: false, exitProgress: 0 };\n              var exitFrames = Math.max(6, Math.round(o.duration * 0.7));\n              var exitStart = Math.max(TOTAL * 30 - exitFrames, o.delay + o.duration);\n              var xt = clamp01((frame - exitStart) / exitFrames), xp = EXIT(xt);\n              var exiting = frame >= exitStart;\n              return { motion: exiting ? 1 - xp : motion, opacity: opacity * EXIT(1 - clamp01(xt / 0.7)), exiting: exiting, exitProgress: xp };\n            }\n\n            var text = str(vars.text, \"Swing into place.\");\n            var el = document.getElementById(\"rti-text\");\n            el.textContent = text;\n            el.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", text);\n            el.style.fontSize = num(vars.font_size, 84, 24, 260) + \"px\";\n            el.style.fontWeight = String(num(vars.font_weight, 700, 100, 900));\n            el.style.color = str(vars.color, \"#f4f4f5\");\n            var degrees = num(vars.degrees, -12, -180, 180), axis = pick(vars.axis, [\"z\", \"x\", \"y\"], \"z\"), persp = num(vars.perspective, 1200, 200, 4000);\n            var scaleFrom = num(vars.scale_from, 0.96, 0.2, 1.5);\n            var o = { duration: num(vars.duration_frames, 30, 4, 120), delay: num(vars.delay_frames, 6, 0, 120), exit: bool(vars.exit, true) };\n            el.style.transformOrigin = pick(vars.origin, [\"center\", \"top\", \"bottom\", \"left\", \"right\", \"top left\", \"top right\", \"bottom left\", \"bottom right\"], \"center\");\n            function draw(frame) {\n              var s = enterExit(frame, o);\n              var rot = degrees * (1 - s.motion), sc = Math.pow(scaleFrom, 1 - s.motion);\n              el.style.opacity = String(s.opacity);\n              el.style.transform = axis === \"z\" ? \"rotate(\" + rot.toFixed(3) + \"deg) scale(\" + sc.toFixed(4) + \")\"\n                : \"perspective(\" + persp + \"px) rotate\" + axis.toUpperCase() + \"(\" + rot.toFixed(3) + \"deg) scale(\" + sc.toFixed(4) + \")\";\n            }\n            drive(\"rotate-in\", draw);\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
